{title: My Jesus, as Thou Wilt}
{artist: Benjamin Schmolck, tr. Jane Borthwick / Carl Maria von Weber}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (My_Jesus_As_Thou_Wilt-Jewett-Weber) and the Cyber Hymnal score (96% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]My Jesus, [A]as Thou wilt!
[D]Oh, may Thy will be mine!
[G]Into [D]Thy hand of love
[D]I [A]would my [D]all re[A]sign;
[D]Through sorrow, [A]or through joy,
[D7]Conduct me as Thine [G]own,
[G]And help me [D]still to say,
[D]My Lord, Thy will__[A7]__ be [D]done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]My Jesus, [A]as Thou wilt!
[D]If needy here and poor,
[G]Give me [D]Thy people’s bread,
[D]Their [A]portion [D]rich and [A]sure.
[D]The manna [A]of Thy Word
[D7]Let my soul feed up[G]on;
[G]And if all [D]else should fail,
[D]My Lord, thy will__[A7]__ be [D]done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]My Jesus, [A]as Thou wilt!
[D]Though seen through many'a tear,
[G]Let not [D]my star of hope
[D]Grow [A]dim or [D]disap[A]pear;
[D]Since Thou on [A]earth hast wept,
[D7]And sorrowed oft a[G]lone,
[G]If I must [D]weep with Thee,
[D]My Lord, Thy will__[A7]__ be [D]done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]My Jesus, [A]as Thou wilt!
[D]All shall be well for me;
[G]Each chang[D]ing future scene
[D]I [A]gladly [D]trust with [A]Thee:
[D]Straight to my [A]home above
[D7]I travel calmly [G]on,
[G]And sing, in [D]life or death,
[D]My Lord, Thy will__[A7]__ be [D]done!
{end_of_verse}
